Package: causalmetrics
Title: Utility Functions and New Methods for Empirical Causal Inference
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R:
    person("Weiheng", "Zhang", email = "weiheng.zhang626@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Data cleaning utilities, descriptive table functions, diagnostics,
    and from-scratch causal estimators for applied empirical research in
    economics and marketing. The current estimator is augmented inverse
    propensity weighting ('est_aipw()') and double/debiased machine learning
    ('est_dml()'); synthetic difference-in-differences is planned. Lecture-note vignettes and paper
    replications document each identification strategy. Attaching the package
    also attaches the standard empirical analysis toolkit (tidyverse,
    data.table, fixest, estimatr, broom, modelsummary, kableExtra).
